  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate that adequate measures would be secured to mitigate noise, pollution and odour arising from the proposed commercial use. The proposal has not demonstrated that neighbouring residential occupiers, particularly those located directly above the premises, would be adequately protected from noise and odour impacts. The development would therefore result in unacceptable adverse impacts on the amenity and living conditions of neighbouring residential occupiers, contrary to Policies LP2 (Development and Amenity), LP38 (&lt;/span&gt;Evening and Night Time Economy),&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;and LP58 (Improving the Environment – Pollution) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020), Policies D13 (Agent of Change) and D14 (Noise) and SI1 (Improving air quality) of&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;the London Plan (2021),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;and Policy P3 (&lt;/span&gt;Living conditions and pollution)&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed hot food takeaway operation, by reason of its close proximity to nearby schools, would contribute to and have an adverse impact upon rising levels of childhood obesity in the borough,&amp;nbsp; contrary to policy E9 (Retail, markets and hot food takeaways) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP9 (Health and Wellbeing) and LP39 (Over-Concentration of Uses) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020), and Policy&amp;nbsp;HC5 (Hot food takeaways) of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed change of use would result in the loss of a public house/drinking establishment with no adequate marketing evidence provided, or evidence to confirm that&amp;nbsp;no other forms of social infrastructure can be provided at the site, contrary to policy HC5 (Supporting London’s culture and creative industries), policy LP8 (Social and Community Infrastructure) of the Local Plan (2020) and policy HC6 (Retention of key community facilities and public service infrastructure) of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;In the absence of a&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Transport Statement to assess the impacts of the proposed operation, particularly delivery drivers related to the hot food takeaway operation, the proposals would have an adverse impact on highway safety and sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Policies T1 (Strategic approach to transport) and T4 (Assessing and mitigating transport impacts) of the London Plan (2021), Hackney Local Plan Policies LP41 (Liveable Neighbourhoods), LP42 (Walking and Cycling) and LP43 (Transport and Development), and Policies TR3 (Locating development in sustainable locations) and TR4 (Assessing transport impacts) of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ]
